doc:aab_judgment_2016_10_14 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Aliens Appeals Board judgment (14 October 2016) - stay of execution of 10 Oct decision"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aliens_office_decisions_2016_10_10 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:aliensAppealsBoard ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_aab_applicants_2016_10_14,
        doc:part_aab_state_2016_10_07 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "By a judgment of 14 October 2016 the Aliens Appeals Board, acting under the extremely urgent procedure, again ordered a stay of execution of the decision of 10 October 2016 refusing to issue the visas, and instructed the Aliens Office to take new decisions, this time giving adequate legal grounds, within 48 hours."@en .

doc:aab_judgment_2016_10_20 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Aliens Appeals Board judgment (20 October 2016) - stay and order to issue laissez-passers/visas"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aliens_office_refusal_2016_10_17 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:aliensAppealsBoard ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_aab_applicants_2016_10_20,
        doc:part_aab_state_2016_10_20 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "By a judgment of 20 October 2016 the Aliens Appeals Board, essentially reiterating the substance of its previous judgments, ordered a stay of execution of the refusal decisions of 17 October 2016. In addition, in view of the imminent danger faced by the applicants, the Belgian State’s persistent refusal to comply with res judicata authority and the importance of ensuring that the remedy was effective, it considered that it was justified to direct the State to issue the applicants, within 48 hours, with laissez-passers or visas, valid for three months."@en .

doc:aab_order_2016_10_07 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Aliens Appeals Board order (7 October 2016) - stay of execution"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aliens_office_refusal_2016_09_13 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:aliensAppealsBoard ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_aab_applicants_2016_10_07,
        doc:part_aab_state_2016_10_07 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 7 October 2016 the Aliens Appeals Board, acting under the extremely urgent procedure, ordered a stay of execution of the refusals by the Aliens Office to grant visas and instructed the Belgian State to take new decisions within 48 hours, giving adequate legal grounds, that is, by giving reasons which took account of the extremely dangerous situation in Syria."@en .

doc:aliens_office_refusal_2016_09_13 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Aliens Office refusal (13 September 2016)"@en ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-09-13"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_applicants_aliens_office_2016_09_13 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 13 September 2016 the Aliens Office, the administrative body responsible for issuing visas (see paragraph 45 below), refused to grant “humanitarian visas” to the applicants and informed them of its decisions by an email of 29 September 2016, transmitted through the visa department of the Belgian embassy in Beirut."@en .

doc:aliens_office_refusal_2016_10_17 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Aliens Office decisions refusing visas (17 October 2016)"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aab_judgment_2016_10_14 ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_applicants_aliens_office_2016_09_13 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 17 October 2016 the Aliens Office again took decisions refusing to issue the visas, citing the same reasons as in the previous refusals."@en .

