    rdfs:label "Enforcement judge at Brussels French-language TPI"@en ;
    echr:hasAuthorityKind echr:AuthorityJudicial ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "the enforcement judge at the Brussels French-language TPI"@en .

doc:brusselsFrenchTpi a echr:DomesticAuthority ;
    rdfs:label "Brussels French-language Court of First Instance (TPI)"@en ;
    echr:hasAuthorityKind echr:AuthorityJudicial ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "the President of the Brussels French-language Court of First Instance (“TPI”)"@en .

doc:brussels_court_of_appeal_2017_06_30 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Brussels Court of Appeal judgment (30 June 2017) - Dutch‑language division: AAB judgment no longer operative"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:court_of_appeal_varied_2016_12_14 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:brusselsCourtOfAppeal ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2017-06-30"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_coa2017_applicants_2017_06_30,
        doc:part_coa2017_state_2017_06_30 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "By a judgment of 30 June 2017 a Dutch-language division of the Court of Appeal held that the Aliens Appeals Boards’ judgment of 20 October 2016 was no longer operative, given that the applicants had not lodged an application to have the visa refusal decisions of 13 September 2016 set aside."@en .

doc:conseilDetat a echr:DomesticAuthority ;
    rdfs:label "Conseil d’État"@en ;
    echr:hasAuthorityKind echr:AuthorityAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "Under section 39/67 of the Aliens Act, an appeal on points of law against the decisions of the Aliens Appeals Board lies to the Conseil d’État ."@en .

doc:part_aab_state_2016_10_07 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "Participation: Belgian State in AAB judgment 14/10/2016"@en,
        "Participation: Belgian State in AAB order 07/10/2016"@en ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideResponding ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "the Belgian State opposed, before the same courts, the granting of visas."@en ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:belgianState .

doc:tpi_order_2016_10_25 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Order by acting president of Brussels French-language TPI (25 October 2016) - urgent measure to comply"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aab_judgment_2016_10_20 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:brusselsFrenchTpi ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-10-25"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_tpi_applicants_2016_10_25,
        doc:part_tpi_state_2016_10_25 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "By an order of 25 October 2016, considering that the failure by the Aliens Office to comply with a judgment of the Aliens Appeals Board, notwithstanding the fact that it had been immediately enforceable, constituted “an unacceptable illegal action”, the acting president of the French-language TPI ordered the State, as an urgent measure, to comply with the Board’s judgment of 20 October 2016, that is, to issue the applicants with visas or laissez-passers , and made the order subject to a penalty payment of 1,000 euros (EUR) per day of delay and per applicant."@en .

doc:aab_dismiss_2017_03_24 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Aliens Appeals Board dismissal (24 March 2017) - application to set decisions aside dismissed"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aliens_office_decisions_2016_10_10 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:aliensAppealsBoard ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2017-03-24"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_aab_applicants_2017_03_24,
        doc:part_aab_state_2017_03_24 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 24 March 2017 the Aliens Appeals Board dismissed the application to have those decisions set aside, finding that the Aliens Office’s decisions of 13 September 2016 (see paragraph 11 above) had become final and that, in consequence, the applicants no longer had standing to challenge the subsequent decisions."@en .

doc:brusselsCourtOfAppeal a echr:DomesticAuthority ;
    rdfs:label "Brussels Court of Appeal"@en ;
    echr:hasAuthorityKind echr:AuthorityJudicial ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "the Brussels Court of Appeal delivered a judgment on 7 December 2016"@en .

doc:brussels_court_of_appeal_2016_12_07 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Brussels Court of Appeal judgment (7 December 2016) - varied order and ordered execution"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:tpi_decision_2016_11_07 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:brusselsCourtOfAppeal ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-12-07"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_appeal_applicants_2016_12_07,
        doc:part_appeal_state_2016_12_07 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On an appeal by the applicants, the Brussels Court of Appeal delivered a judgment on 7 December 2016 varying the order of 7 November 2016. It held that the applicants could rely on the binding and enforceable nature of the contested judgment and on their subjective right to seek compliance and obtain an end to the harm sustained by them as a result of non-execution of the judgment, which constituted “an illegal action” and manifest fault."@en .

doc:court_of_appeal_varied_2016_12_14 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Court of Appeal judgment (14 December 2016) - varied first-instance decision on stay"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:tpi_decision_2016_11_07 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:brusselsCourtOfAppeal ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-12-14"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_cav_applicants_2016_12_14,
        doc:part_cav_state_2016_12_14 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "However, on an appeal by the Belgian State, the court of appeal varied the decision of the first-instance court in a judgment of 14 December 2016. It noted the Belgian State’s intention to raise the difficulties of complying with the judgment of 7 December 2016 with the enforcement judge (“ le juge des saisies ”) and ordered the applicants not to pursue further enforcement proceedings pending a decision by the enforcement judge who was to rule on the validity of the enforcement procedure and the State’s right to restrict the amounts due in respect of penalty payments."@en .

doc:participation_applicants_aliens_office_2016_09_13 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "Participation: applicants in Aliens Office refusal 13/09/2016"@en,
        "Participation: applicants regarding Aliens Office decisions 10/10/2016"@en ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideInitiating ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 13 September 2016 the Aliens Office ... refused to grant “humanitarian visas” to the applicants"@en,
        "the Aliens Office issued new decisions, dated 10 October 2016, refusing to grant the visas"@en ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:applicantsMNAndOthers .

doc:tpi_decision_2016_11_07 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "French-language TPI decision (7 November 2016) - application admissible but unfounded"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:tpi_order_2016_10_25 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:brusselsFrenchTpi ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-11-07"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:part_tpi_applicants_2016_11_07,
        doc:part_tpi_state_2016_11_07 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 7 November 2016 another judge acting as president of the French ‑ language TPI declared their application admissible but unfounded, considering that the Belgian authorities could not be criticised for failing voluntarily to comply with a judgment by the Aliens Appeals Board, even one that was immediately enforceable, if these same authorities intended to challenge the legality of the judgment by pursuing an appeal procedure provided for by law."@en .

doc:aliensAppealsBoard a echr:DomesticAuthority ;
    rdfs:label "Aliens Appeals Board"@en ;
    echr:hasAuthorityKind echr:AuthorityAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "the Aliens Appeals Board – the judicial appeal body against decisions by the Aliens Office (see paragraph 52 below) –, requesting a stay of execution, under the extremely urgent procedure, of the Aliens Office’s decisions of 13 September 2016"@en .

doc:aliens_office_decisions_2016_10_10 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Aliens Office new decisions (10 October 2016) refusing visas"@en ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:aab_order_2016_10_07 ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2016-10-10"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_applicants_aliens_office_2016_09_13 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "As required by the order of the Aliens Appeals Board (see paragraph 15 above), the Aliens Office issued new decisions, dated 10 October 2016, refusing to grant the visas; however, it provided the same reasons as in the previous refusals."@en .

doc:belgianState a echr:Party ;
    rdfs:label "the Belgian State"@en ;
    echr:hasPartyName "the Belgian State"@en ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "For its part, the Belgian State opposed, before the same courts, the granting of visas."@en ;
    echr:isRepresentedBy doc:repEDerriks,
        doc:repINiedlispacher .

doc:applicantsMNAndOthers a echr:NaturalPerson,
        echr:Party ;
    rdfs:label "M.N. and Others (the applicants)"@en ;
    echr:hasPartyName "M.N. and Others"@en ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "on 10 January 2018 by a married couple and their two minor children, all Syrian nationals (“the applicants”)."@en ;
    echr:isRepresentedBy doc:repLLambert,
        doc:repOStein .

